      "summary": "api-gateway GET /api/orders p95 is about 3.08s. Almost all of that time is a DNS lookup of auth.idp.example that the gateway makes before calling orders. Each lookup times out against resolver 10.0.0.2:53, and the gateway retries after about 3s. The orders, catalog and cart services are all fast and healthy. I could not confirm when this started because the time series came back empty.",
      "root_cause": "DNS resolution of auth.idp.example from api-gateway is timing out against resolver 10.0.0.2:53. The first try fails with \"i/o timeout\" and the retry adds about 3s to each GET /api/orders request that does the auth lookup. The lookup does succeed after the retry, which is why requests are slow rather than failing. The delay is in DNS and the resolver, not in any application service.",
